  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts you're likely thinking of are most commonly called the **Columbia PFG Terminal Tackle** shirts (long-sleeve tee style) or the **PFG Bahama** shirts. Here's a quick breakdown of the most popular thin/lightweight options:\n\n1. **PFG Bahama II** \u2013 Featuring lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy relaxed fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun. It's one of the most popular thin PFG button-up styles.\n\n2. **Terminal Tackle** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. Equipped with Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, it dries quickly and manages moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n3. **Tamiami** \u2013 A long-sleeve fishing shirt featuring a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric and UPF 50 sun protection.\n\n4. **Tidal Deflector** \u2013 Great for those who get hot and sweaty on the water, made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology using touch-activated cooling fabric to prevent overheating.\n\nAll of these fall under Columbia's **PFG (Performance Fishing Gear)** line. The PFG line, which stands for Performance Fishing Gear, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style. The **Bahama** and **Terminal Tackle** are generally considered the thinnest and most breathable of the bunch.",
